sieve-filter-v2
; melody-ambitus-v1 for the notes3 family: from the lowest note to the highest is at most the span.
; The state is the lowest note so far and how far above it the highest is.
; On a notes3 line the notes of one pitch, at every level and length, are one run of symbols,
; NOTE(p, 1, 1) to NOTE(p, LEVELS, LONGEST), and the rests another, REST(1) to REST(LONGEST).
id        melody-ambitus-notes3
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes3*
describe  From the lowest note to the highest is at most the span, in semitones.
param     span  int  12  0  48  the widest the melody may be, lowest note to highest, in semitones

states    {1 + PITCHES * (span + 1)}
start     0
accept    0..{PITCHES * (span + 1)}
t 0 @{REST(1)}..@{REST(LONGEST)} 0
for q 1 {PITCHES}
  t 0 @{NOTE(q, 1, 1)}..@{NOTE(q, LEVELS, LONGEST)} {1 + (q - 1) * (span + 1)}
done
for lo 1 {PITCHES}
  for w 0 {span}
    if {lo + w <= PITCHES}
      t {1 + (lo - 1) * (span + 1) + w} @{REST(1)}..@{REST(LONGEST)} {1 + (lo - 1) * (span + 1) + w}
      for q {max(1, lo + w - span)} {min(PITCHES, lo + span)}
        t {1 + (lo - 1) * (span + 1) + w} @{NOTE(q, 1, 1)}..@{NOTE(q, LEVELS, LONGEST)} {1 + (min(lo, q) - 1) * (span + 1) + max(lo + w, q) - min(lo, q)}
      done
    fi
  done
done
end
